REPORT D
P0214 Directory entries inherit Deflated without an encoded empty stream. src/write.rs:1450. Calling add_directory with FileOptions configured for Deflated writes a directory header with that method, then clears writing_to_file without emitting or finishing an empty deflate stream. The resulting zero-byte compressed payload is not a valid Deflated entry, so reopening the archive and reading that directory returns a decompression error. Reusing ordinary file options to add directory entries therefore creates unreadable directories.


P0215 The release passes its existing unit and integration tests in the configurations checked, but public-API regression probes found substantial correctness gaps in copying, ZIP64, streaming, extraction, and metadata handling. Findings: 2 High, 18 Medium, and 5 Low. Resource-limit terminations are reported separately and are not treated as defects.


P0216 The original crate was not edited. Reproducers and generated fixtures are retained in the [scratch harness](/work/tmp/zip-review/Cargo.toml). Test names below refer to that harness unless stated otherwise.


