P0227 Raw copying loses ZipCrypto encryption state


P0228 [src/read.rs:1833](/work/crate/src/read.rs:1833), [src/write.rs:1316](/work/crate/src/write.rs:1316).


P0229 An untouched raw copy should preserve encryption metadata. Instead, `file.options()` loses the ZipCrypto encrypted flag while ciphertext is copied unchanged. Readers consequently treat the copied bytes as plaintext.


P0230 Executed evidence: `raw_copy_zipcrypto_retains_encryption` observed `encrypted() == false` after reopening. Source inspection confirms that password handling then discards the supplied password. Fix: preserve raw encryption flags independently of options that request new encryption.


P0231 Raw copying accepts streams whose original bytes are unavailable


P0232 [src/write.rs:1336](/work/crate/src/write.rs:1336).


P0233 The copy operation retains the original sizes and checksum but copies only the remaining underlying bytes. Reading one byte beforehand can also discard unread buffered bytes when extracting the underlying reader. Opening an AES entry for decryption already consumes its encryption header.


P0234 Executed evidence: raw copying returned success, but `copy_before_and_after_read_reports_errors_instead_of_damaged_output` subsequently failed checksum validation; `raw_copy_decrypted_aes_entry` failed with `InvalidPassword`. Fix: enforce an untouched raw-reader state before writing, reject unsupported states, and verify the copied length.


P0235 Raw copying discards promised metadata


P0236 [src/write.rs:1316](/work/crate/src/write.rs:1316), [src/read.rs:1836](/work/crate/src/read.rs:1836).


P0237 The documented operation copies metadata, but reconstruction through `SimpleFileOptions` drops comments, extra fields, and special-file mode bits. A copied symlink becomes a regular file containing its target text.


P0238 Executed evidence: `raw_copy_preserves_symlink_type`, `raw_copy_preserves_extra_fields`, and `raw_copy_preserves_comment` failed. Fix: preserve source metadata directly, changing only fields explicitly requested by the copy operation.


